areia_texto = No target and no budget. Compare two scenarios with the same random numbers. Nothing here counts toward the grade.
limite_cola = Without a server, nothing prevents looking things up. The submission carries the decisions and the signed attempts, and the teacher simulates again: editing the file does not change the grade and leaves the change visible.
prova_texto = The draw uses the recorded seed, among the missions of the open package. The student gets the exam with no reference, no hints and no answer key, with a time window, a time limit and counted runs. Grading happens here, with the exam rebuilt from the seed.
desafio_texto = The scoreboard uses the last grading: the attempt that counts for each student up to the deadline, by grade and then by cost. When the intervals of the indicators overlap, the students appear tied. The class sees only the nickname. Each team submits one solution (the attempt that counts among the members' attempts) and they run in the same factory, with the same random numbers.
programa_texto = If you are in your company's Lean Six Sigma program, point to the program folder. Each solved mission then records "practiced" in your competence map, in the tools tied to it. The record uses your UTSim Seis Sigma identity on this computer.
